<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19353" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gĕbenna</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cĕbenna</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cĕven-na</span></b> , ae, f.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a chain of
				mountains in Gaul</i>, <i>the Cevennes</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G. 7,
				8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">56</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 4,
				5, § 31</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 16, 31, §
			105</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 25</span></i>.—In
				plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gĕbennae</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 5,
			6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 1, 435</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Deriv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gĕbennĭcus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cĕb-</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cĕv-</span></b> ), a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the Cevennes</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">montes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mel.
					2, 5, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
